# Version bumping

When the user asks to **bump the version** or **increase the build number**, use `tool/bump_version.sh` — do not edit `pubspec.yaml` or version files manually.

Default bump type is **build** (increments `x.y.z+build` build number only).

```bash
# Bump build number only (most common)
bash tool/bump_version.sh build

# Bump + commit
bash tool/bump_version.sh build --commit

# Bump + commit + push
bash tool/bump_version.sh build --commit --push
```

Use `patch`, `minor`, or `major` only when the user explicitly asks for a semver bump — not for routine build-number increases.

For release tagging (TestFlight / Play Store), use `tool/release_mobile_tags.sh` instead; it delegates to `tool/bump_version.sh` when `--bump` is passed.
